From 4880b6f28b9878ee0d9a353419ad4347855b2331 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: legsmechanical <joshgaine@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 10:01:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] feat(fx): send FX per-set auto-persist + editor fixes

UI side of send FX Phase 2:
- Per-set auto-persist: saveSendFxChainConfig/restoreSendFxFromFiles write and
  reload send_fx_<bus>_<slot>.json + send_fx_meta.json (per-set return levels),
  mirroring the master FX per-set files. Hooked into the editor save dispatch,
  shadow_save_state_now, init, SET_CHANGED restore, and set-duplicate copy.
  Sends now recall across set changes; empty/new sets clear stale send slots.
- Dissolver / no-hierarchy modules on sends: the send hierarchy editor now treats
  a send as an FX-bus component (hierEditorIsMasterFx path) so the param engine
  builds send_fx:* keys instead of the chain-slot convention; select uses the
  parsed getMasterFxHierarchy with a module-browser fallback.
- FX bus picker Back now exits to Move native (shadow_request_exit); the old
  exitShadowUI() was undefined and silently threw.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
